{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03083",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 3.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.26,
      "end_seconds": 11.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Hmm, hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.87,
      "end_seconds": 14.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.73,
      "end_seconds": 24.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.72,
      "text": "I wanted to get a tight chest at work looked at. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.45,
      "end_seconds": 29.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.31,
      "end_seconds": 36.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, ever since... since last night, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.06,
      "end_seconds": 41.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.16,
      "end_seconds": 45.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "It's, It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.43,
      "end_seconds": 49.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.15,
      "end_seconds": 60.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "It usually comes with wheeze at work. Oh, and itchy eyes at work. That's been about the same, ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.83,
      "end_seconds": 67.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.1,
      "end_seconds": 85.23,
      "duration_seconds": 16.13,
      "text": "Honestly, once or twice a day. The wheeze at work? That's been for about a month. Erm, about wheeze at work, spray paint and work definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.26,
      "end_seconds": 93.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Have you had a tight chest at work before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.43,
      "end_seconds": 103.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Ah, yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.91,
      "end_seconds": 122.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fever, ankle swelling, coughing up blood or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.74,
      "end_seconds": 131.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "No fever, ankle swelling, coughing up blood or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.14,
      "end_seconds": 134.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.05,
      "end_seconds": 137.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.64,
      "end_seconds": 141.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.03,
      "end_seconds": 143.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.91,
      "end_seconds": 150.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.85,
      "end_seconds": 153.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Yes, naproxen. I get stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.74,
      "end_seconds": 157.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.52,
      "end_seconds": 161.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Yes, an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.88,
      "end_seconds": 164.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.7,
      "end_seconds": 168.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I have gout, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.53,
      "end_seconds": 173.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.63,
      "end_seconds": 184.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "It's bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day. I take febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.59,
      "end_seconds": 192.54,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.24,
      "end_seconds": 196.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.89,
      "end_seconds": 200.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.19,
      "end_seconds": 205.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.57,
      "end_seconds": 208.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.93,
      "end_seconds": 213.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.12,
      "end_seconds": 217.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.31,
      "end_seconds": 222.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.51,
      "end_seconds": 226.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.54,
      "end_seconds": 230.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Just a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.35,
      "end_seconds": 243.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.34,
      "end_seconds": 254.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.63,
      "end_seconds": 280.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.48,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.9, respiratory rate 14. And SpO2 97 percent on room air, BP is 115 over 73, pulse is 84 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.9,
      "end_seconds": 285.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.17,
      "end_seconds": 288.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.62,
      "end_seconds": 295.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.53,
      "end_seconds": 297.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.55,
      "end_seconds": 300.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.98,
      "end_seconds": 320.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "There is a little wheeze at the end of each breath out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.04,
      "end_seconds": 341.51,
      "duration_seconds": 18.47,
      "text": "You can relax now. Okay, so my impression is this: I'd lean towards occupational asthma. Record peak flows at work and at home for four weeks. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.18,
      "end_seconds": 346.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Erm, um, thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}